Subject: Cantor Succeeding SOP Review Admission P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] 386463cf-c8c7-4cef-9763-5dd768954b72
@ [canonical_uuid] ff7c9404-2676-4c41-ae98-419445b6ec45

& [Decision]
  + implement pure SWA-06B1 review admission before any physical source persistence or activation

& [Why]
  + SWA-06A already preserves source and emits exact proposal correspondence but cannot distinguish a separately signed review from self-assertion
  + existing Ed25519 support can close cryptographic integrity and key-possession correspondence with no dependency delta
  + policy governance semantic competence filesystem persistence activation recovery and rollback require separate physical evidence and must not be inferred

& [Rejected]
  + infer SWA-05 writer-host selection from desktop use
  + let Cantor generate the reviewer key or sign its own proposal
  + call supplied content digests a satisfaction signature
  + treat cryptographic signature validity as semantic truth
  + write directly into source_documents or activate a current SOP in this seam
  + use a synthetic fixture as production trust

& [ExpectedProductEffect]
  + a second agent or operator can produce one exact signed review package that Cantor verifies deterministically
  + the next physical activation seam receives a closed admission receipt and explicit remaining obligations rather than an unauthenticated proposal
